### Task 1: *Not synced* can be told apart from *No run open*

The server does not know about a run that never synced, so an account whose runs are all local would read *No run open* — true and useless. It does know whether the account has **any** owned, unended session. That is enough to say something better.

**Files:**

- Modify: `hosted/infra/lib/handlers/ws.ts` (`heldRuns`, `tellDecks` from Plan A Task 3)
- Test: `hosted/infra/test/ws.test.ts`

**Interfaces:**

- Consumes: `heldRuns`, `tellDecks` from Plan A.
- Produces: the `runs` message gains `any: boolean` — whether the account has any owned, unended, synced run at all.

- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**

```ts
it("says whether the account has any synced run at all", async () => {
  const live = memoryLive();
  const posted: Array<[string, string]> = [];
  const poster: Poster = { post: async (id, data) => (posted.push([id, data]), "ok") };
  // manifest for user_a is empty in this deps
  const deps = depsWith({ live, poster, sessionsOf: {} });
  await route({ requestContext: { routeKey: "$connect", connectionId: "deck1" }, queryStringParameters: { token: "good", as: "deck" } }, deps);
  expect(JSON.parse(posted.at(-1)![1])).toEqual({ t: "runs", runs: [], any: false });
});
```

- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**

Run: `npm test -w hosted/infra -- ws`
Expected: FAIL — `any` is absent.

- [ ] **Step 3: Carry it**

Change `heldRuns` to return both:

```ts
const heldRuns = async (sub: string): Promise<{ runs: HeldRun[]; any: boolean }> => {
  const { sessions } = await deps.store.manifest(sub);
  const mine = sessions
    .filter((p) => p.role === "owner" && !p.deletedAt && !p.endedAt)
    .sort((a, b) => (a.updatedAt < b.updatedAt ? 1 : a.updatedAt > b.updatedAt ? -1 : 0));
  const recent = mine.slice(0, 20);
  const held = await Promise.all(recent.map(async (p) => ((await deps.live.watchers(p.id)).some(writes) ? p : null)));
  return {
    // `any` is the difference between an account whose runs are all local
    // and one that has nothing open: the key says "Not synced" for the
    // first and "No run open" for the second, and only this end can tell.
    any: mine.length > 0,
    runs: held
      .filter((p): p is (typeof recent)[number] => p !== null)
      .map((p) => ({ id: p.id, ...(p.name ? { name: p.name } : {}), ...(p.packTitle ? { packTitle: p.packTitle } : {}), held: true as const })),
  };
};
```

and in `tellDecks`: `const line = JSON.stringify({ t: "runs", ...(await heldRuns(sub)) });`

Declare `type HeldRun = { id: string; name?: string; packTitle?: string; held: true }` above `route`.

- [ ] **Step 4: Run the tests and commit**

```bash
npm test -w hosted/infra && npm run typecheck
git add hosted/infra/lib/handlers/ws.ts hosted/infra/test/ws.test.ts
git commit -m "feat(live): a deck can tell nothing synced from nothing open"
```

